meta {
  name: Turn semantic search off
  type: http
  seq: 37
}

patch {
  url: {{api}}/bonds/{{bondId}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

script:pre-request {
  // The PATCH is conditional (doc 06 section 1): the bond's ETag, as you read it now, goes in If-Match.
  const axios = require("axios");
  const bond = await axios.get(`${bru.getEnvVar("api")}/bonds/${bru.getVar("bondId") ?? bru.getEnvVar("bondId")}`, {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${bru.getVar("accessToken")}` },
  });
  req.setHeader("If-Match", bond.headers["etag"]);
}

body:json {
  {
    "semanticSearchEnabled": false
  }
}

docs {
  Turns semantic search off for the bond, for both of you, on your own say (FR-204, ADR-0054). 200 with the bond. Within seconds every vector made of your bond's entries is deleted, and from that moment no word of the bond is sent to the embedding provider: search and Remember when find by words alone.

  Only false is accepted here; true is 422 on semanticSearchEnabled (ASSERT_FALSE). Turning it back on needs both of you: Turn semantic search on. It is also accepted on a bond that has ended, where nothing else is (provisional, the owner to confirm).
}
